# Single source of truth for every version this project pins.
#
# Read by:
#   - the Makefile          (`include`; drives `go run <tool>@$(VERSION)` and uv)
#   - docker compose        (the Makefile passes --env-file, build args follow)
#   - plugin/build.sh       (sources this file directly)
#
# Nothing else may hardcode a version. Bump here and every consumer follows.

# Not listed: the Go version. `go` in go.mod is the single source of truth,
# because that directive must be a literal and cannot be templated. Every
# consumer derives it with `sed -n 's/^go //p' go.mod`.

# --- Go tooling ---
GOFUMPT_VERSION=v0.11.0
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=v2.13.2
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.7.0

# --- Python tooling ---
# The apworld runs inside Archipelago's interpreter, so nothing is installed
# from here. uv only ever runs these two, in a throwaway environment: the
# linter, and the drop shadow under the window screenshots.
RUFF_VERSION=0.16.6
PILLOW_VERSION=12.3.0


# --- The stack ---
# Archipelago releases break apworlds. This is the version the world was
# written against and the one the image installs.
ARCHIPELAGO_VERSION=0.6.7

# SourceMod ships the compiler; the version also decides which natives exist.
SOURCEMOD_BRANCH=1.12
SOURCEMOD_VERSION=1.12.0-git7253

# Metamod:Source loads SourceMod. The Docker image's base ships it; a Windows
# install from steamcmd does not, so the launcher installs it.
MMSOURCE_BRANCH=1.12
MMSOURCE_VERSION=1.12.0-git1226

# REST in Pawn: the plugin's only extension.
RIPEXT_VERSION=1.3.2

# --- Server mods a community mission can require ---
# gamedata/server_mods.go is the catalog: which keys community.json may name
# and which platforms have a build. The versions are here, as every pin is.
#
# SigMod (rafradek/sigsegv-mvm), Linux only upstream. The image stages it and
# the entrypoint installs it when SRCDS_MODS names it. The checksum is the
# release's package-linux.zip; a build that fetches something else stops.
SIGSEGV_MVM_VERSION=20250703
SIGSEGV_MVM_SHA256=4967cc2c4765bdd5508ac866603a88746d6d24a1022cc64703030487cf904426

# --- The MvM defender bots ---
# Valve tunes every wave for six defenders, so a solo or small-team run needs
# the empty RED slots filled with bots that play. Nothing prebuilt covers this:
# the extensions ship no binary we can use, and one dependency has no license
# on its release. So the image builds all seven from source, patched in-tree.
# deploy/patches/ holds the patches, and its README says why each exists.

# The stock library the mod compiles against.
#
# The mod itself is not here. It is m-this/tf2-mvm-bots-go, a Go module that
# holds the Go authoring the bots' decisions, the generator that turns it into
# SourcePawn, and the plugin tree that compiles: the go.mod requirement is the
# pin and `go get` is how it moves. A line here would be a second place to say
# which version this build runs, and two places to say one thing is one place
# to be wrong.
SM_STOCK_OFFICERSPY_REF=main

# spcomp 1.12.0-git7246 segfaults on the defender mod (upstream issue #5). This
# is the compiler the mod's own CI uses, and it builds it. Our plugin keeps
# SOURCEMOD_VERSION above; the two compilers coexist.
DEFENDERBOTS_SOURCEMOD_VERSION=1.12.0-git7164

# The two compiled extensions. Actions stays at v3.9.2: v4.0.0's TF2 source was
# never ported to the new processor API and does not compile.
CBASENPC_VERSION=1.15.4.126
ACTIONS_VERSION=v3.9.2

# The three gamedata plugins, and the stock library two of them need.
# TF Econ Data is a tag, not master: master calls a stocksoup stock that no
# release has.
TF2ATTRIBUTES_VERSION=v1.7.5
TFECONDATA_VERSION=0.19.1.5
TF2UTILS_VERSION=master
STOCKSOUP_REF=master

# The build inputs for the two extensions. AMBuild resolves the SDK from
# hl2sdk-tf2 on disk; none of this is the Valve 2025 SDK drop.
HL2SDK_BRANCH=tf2
SOURCEMOD_SRC_BRANCH=1.12-dev
METAMOD_SRC_BRANCH=master

# goversioninfo turns the launcher's manifest, icon and version strings into a
# .syso the linker picks up. Without the manifest the window gets Windows 95
# controls and a blurry font; without the version strings the exe has no
# CompanyName or FileVersion, which is one of the things Defender scores on.
GOVERSIONINFO_VERSION=v1.7.0

# --- The book ---
# honkit is the maintained fork of GitBook 3. It reads docs/SUMMARY.md as it
# already stands, which is the whole reason it is the one that builds the book.
HONKIT_VERSION=6.2.2
